"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[1598],{11598:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"08-iis-i-nalogi","title":"Lesson 08. IIS-3 and Taxes: The Investor\'s Tax Shield","sourceFingerprint":"c5a7a82f92e2717716864c08e6c476cd51d97ac11940b928e81fb741a388ff99","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"# Chapter 8. The Investor\'s Tax Shield: How to Retain Profits Using IIS-3 and Holding Tax Benefits"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"> \\"Profit from a successful trade is always fraught with market uncertainty. Tax optimization is the only way to increase portfolio returns with a one-hundred percent guarantee and zero risk.\\"  \\n> — *MakeCash Book, Volume II: \\"Capital Protection: 20 Years Against Inflation\\"*"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"⏱ *Thoughtful reading time: 6 minutes*"},{"id":"b004","markdown":"Beginner investors often overlook tax costs: the broker deducts thirteen percent unnoticed upon withdrawal of funds or at the end of December, creating the illusion of negligible losses. However, over a distance of ten to twenty years, unoptimized personal income tax (PIT) can take away up to a third of the final compound interest."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"Russian financial legislation provides retail investors with powerful tools to preserve returns. To avoid surrendering unnecessary amounts to the state, it is enough to competently choose the trading account type and maintain investment discipline."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"## Anatomy of Investment PIT: What the Federal Tax Service Takes and How Much"},{"id":"b007","markdown":"Any financial result from operations in the stock market is subject to taxation according to a standard progressive scale:"},{"id":"b008","markdown":"* **13%** — the base rate if the investor\'s total income for the calendar year does not exceed **2.4 million rubles**;\\n* **15%** — the rate on the amount exceeding the specified threshold of 2.4 million ₽ (for higher incomes, the scale rises up to the maximum brackets)."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"Three key revenue items are subject to fiscal burden:"},{"id":"b010","markdown":"1. **Capital gains:** the positive difference between the sale price of a security (stock, bond, exchange-traded fund unit) and its purchase price, net of brokerage and exchange commissions.\\n2. **Coupon income:** payouts on bonds of any type, including sovereign debt securities (OFZ).\\n3. **Dividend stream:** company distributions to shareholders (tax is withheld at the time of payout by the issuer)."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"A broker within Russian jurisdiction acts as a **tax agent**. This eliminates the need to file a tax return manually: the brokerage firm independently nets profits and losses, withholds tax when withdrawing rubles from the balance, or debits it based on December results."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"> **The loss offsetting rule:** losing trades reduce the tax base. If over a year you made 60,000 ₽ on one position and booked a loss of 20,000 ₽ on another, PIT will be levied solely on net profit — on 40,000 ₽ (the tax will be 5,200 ₽ instead of 7,800 ₽). Within a single broker, offsetting occurs automatically; the financial results of different platforms can be consolidated by filing a 3-NDFL tax return."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"## Long-Term Holding Tax Exemption (LDV): A Reward for Patience"},{"id":"b014","markdown":"If an investor does not engage in speculation and holds assets in their portfolio for more than three years, the law exempts the positive result from the sale of such instruments from PIT."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"* **Financial limit:** up to **3,000,000 ₽ of net profit per each full year of ownership** is exempt. Accordingly, for three years of continuous holding, the limit will be **9,000,000 ₽**, and for five years — **15,000,000 ₽**.\\n* **Eligibility criteria:** assets must be traded on domestic exchange auctions (stocks, bonds, BPIFs) and purchased after January 1, 2014.\\n* **Calculation specifics:** the three-year timer ticks separately for each purchased lot under the FIFO rule (first in, first out)."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"⚠️ *Important restriction:* LDV neutralizes taxes only on market value appreciation. Incoming dividends and coupons in a standard brokerage account are subject to PIT in the standard manner without exemptions."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"## IIS-3: The Flagship Account with Dual Tax Protection"},{"id":"b018","markdown":"The type-3 individual investment account (valid for all accounts opened from 2024 onward) combined the advantages of older IIS formats. While previously one had to choose between a tax refund on contributions and a profit exemption, IIS-3 provides **both preferences simultaneously**."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"```\\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│                         IIS-3 BENEFIT ARCHITECTURE                     │\\n├──────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│    INFLOW DEDUCTION (ON TOP-UPS) │        OUTFLOW TAX EXEMPTION        │\\n│                                  │                                     │\\n│  13% refund of the top-up amount │  Full exemption from PIT on         │\\n│  (up to 52,000 ₽ annually on a   │  profits from trades and coupons    │\\n│  base up to 400,000 ₽; up to     │  upon closing the account.          │\\n│  60,000 ₽ at a 15% PIT rate).    │  Tax-free profit limit —            │\\n│  Official income required.       │  up to 30,000,000 ₽ for whole term. │\\n└──────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────┘\\n```"},{"id":"b020","markdown":"### Key Parameters and Restrictions of IIS-3:"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"* **Account lifespan:** for contracts registered in 2024–2026, the minimum holding period to preserve tax preferences is **5 years**. Starting in 2027, this threshold will gradually increase by one year annually until it reaches 10 years.\\n* **Prohibition of withdrawals:** partial capital withdrawal is not allowed. Early closure cancels all received deductions: they must be returned to the state along with accrued penalties, and the broker will withhold standard tax on the financial result. The only statutory exception is withdrawing funds to pay for expensive medical services from an approved list.\\n* **Closing rule:** no contribution deduction is granted in the year the account is closed. It is optimal to close the contract at the beginning of the next calendar year (in January–February).\\n* **Instruments:** only Russian securities are permitted (OFZ, corporate bonds, stocks, exchange-traded funds of Russian management companies).\\n* **Multi-accounts:** an investor is permitted to concurrently hold a pool of up to three IIS-3 accounts with different brokers.\\n* **Combined limit:** the contribution ceiling for receiving the annual deduction (400 000 ₽) is shared across IIS-3, the Long-Term Savings Program (PDS), and voluntary contributions to NPFs.\\n* **Insurance:** starting January 1, 2026, a state asset insurance mechanism of up to **1.4 million ₽** takes effect for IIS-3 accounts in the event of intermediary license revocation or bankruptcy (voluntary participation among licensed brokers; insurance does not cover market price drawdown risks)."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"## Capital Allocation Map by Time Horizons"},{"id":"b023","markdown":"Do not allocate all free cash into a single account. Balance your assets based on the time horizon when you will need them:"},{"id":"b024","markdown":"| Goal Horizon | Recommended Instrument | Tax Strategy |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Short-term (up to 1–3 years)** + emergency fund | Bank deposits, high-yield savings accounts, liquidity funds (LQDT) | Tax incentives will not have time to activate. The priority is instant access and zero risk of capital drawdown. |\\n| **Medium-term (from 3 to 5 years)** | Standard brokerage account | Buying reliable assets without selling for at least 3 years to automatically activate LDV. Freedom to withdraw funds on any day without penalties. |\\n| **Long-term (from 5 years and up)** | Individual Investment Account (IIS-3) | Maximum tax boost: refund of paid personal income tax on contributions plus tax-free coupon income and capital gains up to 30 million ₽. |"},{"id":"b025","markdown":"## \uD83E\uDDEE Calculation in the Margins"},{"id":"b026","markdown":"**Objective:** Compare the results of a conservative capital allocation in an IIS-3 versus a regular brokerage account over a five-year horizon."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"**Input parameters:**\\n* Annual contribution: **400 000 ₽** at the beginning of each year (total contributed: 2 000 000 ₽).\\n* Investor\'s personal income tax rate on official salary: **13%**.\\n* Portfolio\'s average annual yield (OFZ + corporate bonds): **10% per annum**.\\n* Holding period: **5 years**."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"```\\nACCUMULATION DYNAMICS (IIS-3 VS. BROKERAGE ACCOUNT):"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"Year 1: Contribution 400 000 ₽ → Capital by year-end: 440 000 ₽\\nYear 2: Contribution 400 000 ₽ + refund 52 000 ₽ → Capital with interest: 976 000 ₽\\nYear 3: Contribution 400 000 ₽ + refund 52 000 ₽ → Capital with interest: 1 565 600 ₽\\nYear 4: Contribution 400 000 ₽ + refund 52 000 ₽ → Capital with interest: 2 214 160 ₽\\nYear 5: Contribution 400 000 ₽ + refund 52 000 ₽ → Capital with interest: 2 927 576 ₽\\n```"},{"id":"b030","markdown":"* **Direct personal income tax refund from the state:** 52 000 ₽ \xd7 5 years = **260 000 ₽**.\\n* **Profit from reinvestment and interest:** approx. 927 576 ₽.\\n* **Tax upon account closure after 5 years:**\\n  * On *IIS-3*: **0 ₽** (coupons and capital gains fall within the 30 million ₽ limit).\\n  * On a *regular account* (without coupon tax exemption): a 13% tax on the coupon cash flow would take over **120 000 ₽**, while the 260 000 ₽ refund would not exist at all."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"**Total net profit from using IIS-3:** the investor receives over **380 000 ₽** in net tax advantage with an identical set of securities."}],"terms":[{"id":"iis-3","term":"IIS-3","definition":"an individual investment account that combines a contribution tax deduction and an exemption of income from personal income tax."},{"id":"ldv","term":"LDV (Long-Term Ownership Relief)","definition":"a tax relief for holding securities for more than 3 years."},{"id":"nalogovyj-agent","term":"Tax agent","definition":"a Russian broker that independently calculates and withholds the client\'s personal income tax."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"q1","q":"An investor opened a standard brokerage account in March 2024, purchased index fund units for 300,000 ₽, and completely sold them in May 2025 for 420,000 ₽. No other transactions were made. How will the broker calculate the tax?","options":["No tax is withheld because the profit did not exceed 3 million rubles.","The broker will withhold 13% on the profit of 120,000 ₽ (15,600 ₽), since the continuous holding period was less than three years.","An increased tax of 15% must be paid for short-term speculation."],"correct":1,"explanation":""},{"id":"q2","q":"What key advantage does an IIS-3 holder gain compared to a standard brokerage account regarding bond coupon income?","options":["Under IIS-3, coupons are paid at double the rate through government subsidies.","On a regular account, tax on coupons is always withheld, whereas on IIS-3, upon closing the account after the 5-year period expires, coupon income is exempt from personal income tax (within a 30 million ₽ limit of total profit).","Coupons on an IIS-3 are exempt from tax only when purchasing high-risk equities."],"correct":1,"explanation":""},{"id":"q3","q":"An employee with an official salary opened an IIS-3 in March 2024 and deposits 400,000 ₽ annually. In the fall of 2026, he urgently needed money to buy a car and closed the account. What are the tax consequences?","options":["He can withdraw the money without penalties, since he maintained the account for more than 2 years.","The funds are confiscated by the state for breach of contract.","He will have to return all previously received contribution deductions plus pay penalties, and the broker will withhold personal income tax on the earned investment income."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);